# ── WinZapp: project-specific ignores ────────────────────────────────────────

# User data / secrets (generated at runtime, never committed)
# Bare data/ (repo root, not client/data/) covers dev-mode runs launched
# from the repo root instead of client/ — app_paths.data_path() resolves
# against the current working directory in dev mode, so which one gets
# used depends on where the process was actually started from.
data/
client/data/media_failed.json
client/data/messages.db
client/data/messages.db-shm
client/data/messages.db-wal
client/data/settings.json
client/data/settings_default.json
client/data/secret.key
client/data/media/
client/data/voice_messages/
client/data/log/
# Per-account and install-global runtime data (multi-account: one subfolder per
# account id holding its own media/voice_messages/db/token — never committed)
client/WinZapp.spec
client/data/accounts/
client/data/global/
client/logs/
/log/


# Bundled Node.js runtime (binary distribution, ~50 MB)
# The zip pattern is deliberately version-agnostic: it used to name one exact
# file (node-v24.15.0-win-x64.zip), which stopped covering anything the moment
# the version moved — node_download.py pins 22.22.2, and the CI cache key names
# v24.15.0. Any hand-downloaded zip of a version other than the one hardcoded
# here was not ignored at all, leaving a ~30 MB binary one `git add .` away
# from the history.
/client/node/
/client/node*.zip

# WPPConnect Server runtime (downloaded dynamically via setup_api.py)
/client/api/

# Permanent, always-tracked mirror of the same custom patch files above —
# the single source of truth setup_api.py / ApiSetupDialog restore from
# after a clone/re-clone, independent of whatever (if anything) happens to
# still be on disk in client/api/ at that moment. Before this existed, a
# clean re-clone (or the user deleting client/api/ before reinstalling —
# reported live as regressing to a version of these patches from months
# earlier, silently, with no error) had nothing reliable to restore from:
# the "stash whatever's currently in client/api/src/ before wiping it"
# fallback is worthless when client/api/ was already gone. NEVER add a
# pattern above that would catch this path — it must always be tracked.
!/client/api_patches/
/client/api_patches/dist/
/build/
/dist/

